# Shell scripts must keep LF wherever they were authored. `scripts/install.sh` is served from
# the CDN and run by `curl | bash`; a CRLF committed from a Windows worktree makes the very
# first line fail with `$'\r': command not found`, on every user's machine at once.
*.sh text eol=lf

# A script with a shebang line that a test imports through Vite must keep LF. With core.autocrlf on
# Windows the checkout gives `#!/usr/bin/env node` a trailing CR and Vite stops on it with
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" (packages/cli/tests/check-cli-release.test.ts).
*.mjs text eol=lf
